Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 20:07:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02041/11362] [conductor] Pre-gate block: PHASE A3 (DEPTH; the
 fresh-pool fallback; gated_on A1 family_split_feasible==false) -- build a
 FRESH ARC-TGI family-disjoint candidate pool, then run the cross-family
 beats-vote gate. Runs ONLY when A1 finds the existing 52-task pool too
 family-concentrated for a powered held-out-family test. Use the ARC-TGI
 task-family generators (arXiv:2603.05099; 461 generators covering ARC-Mini +
 ARC-AGI-1) and/or expand candidate coverage across MORE cached source
 families to build a larger family-diverse pool with materialized family_id +
 exact target_hash per row. Train the set-encoder on train-families, test on
 HELD-OUT families. Keep ORIGINAL ARC tasks as a held-out sanity read (ARC-TGI
 warning: generator data can become its own distribution -- report
 generator-family and original-task metrics SEPARATELY). Report
 cross_family_delta + CI95 + held_out_family_n + oracle@K. Emit
 cross_family_win_holds BARE bool. verifier_is_oracle=false. HARD-CAP the
 build to the 80-min window; honest partial is fine.

1 of 1 gate(s) failed; first failure: exp4270-arc-family-provenance-recovery.family_split_feasible (actual=True == expected=False)

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
